    'Ten, and then the three more, eleven, twelve, thirteen. Ten and three is thirteen.',
    'Mia tried more. Ten and five was eleven, twelve, thirteen, fourteen, fifteen. Ten and seven was seventeen.',
    'Every teen number is ten and some more. The carton is the ten, and the loose eggs are the some.',
