    'It was a school, said Grandma, my school. She pointed at a desk by the window and said that one was hers.',
    'Then: a chalkboard, a bell on a rope, and one room for every grade. Lena tried to picture all the kids together.',
    'Now: a screen, a buzzer, many rooms and a gym. Lena\'s school had all of that.',
    'Grandma was a girl then, and Lena is a girl now. A timeline puts them in order, then on the left and now on the right.',
