STORIES['healthy-relationships-9'] = {
  about: 'an older cousin who left a controlling relationship, the signs she missed, what she looks for now, and a boundary set with a friend',
  more: [{ serial: 'S3549', after: 1, alt: 'A young woman telling her teenage cousin a story over hot chocolate' }, { serial: 'S3550', after: 2, alt: 'A young woman listening as her best friend talks to her gently' }, { serial: 'S3551', after: 3, alt: 'A young woman writing what healthy relationships share on a notepad' }, { serial: 'S3552', after: 4, alt: 'A teenage girl telling a friend that reading her texts has to stop' }, { serial: 'S3553', after: 5, alt: 'Two teenage friends laughing together at lunch' }],
  title: 'What my cousin told me', art: 'S3548', cast: [],
  alt: 'A teenage girl and her older cousin sitting at a kitchen table with mugs',
  words: [
    'Maya was sixteen when her cousin Rosa, who was twenty-four, came to stay for a week after ending a two-year relationship. Rosa had always seemed like the most confident person in the family, so Maya was surprised by how quiet she was.',
    'Over hot chocolate, Rosa explained. At first her boyfriend had seemed devoted, texting all day and wanting every evening together. Slowly he started checking her phone, getting angry when she saw her friends, and telling her what to wear.',
    '"It never felt like control at the time," Rosa said. "It felt like love that was a little too strong." In the end, her best friend noticed that Rosa had stopped coming to anything, and said so, gently, more than once.',
    'Rosa told Maya what she looks for now: someone who respects her friends, keeps his word, listens when she disagrees and takes no for an answer the first time. Healthy relationships, she said, feel like good friendships with more at stake.',
    'That weekend, Maya thought about her own friendships. One friend had a habit of reading her texts over her shoulder and sulking when Maya spent time with other people. Maya told her, kindly but clearly, that it had to stop.',
    'Her friend was embarrassed, then grateful. Maya realized that boundaries were not walls. They were a way of telling people how to stay close to you. When Rosa left at the end of the week, she hugged Maya and said she was proud of her.',
  ],
};
STORIES['safety-and-abuse-9'] = {
  about: 'a scout with thousands of followers, a gift card and a secret, the warning signs of grooming, and a mother who called the hotline',
  more: [{ serial: 'S3555', after: 1, alt: 'A gift card notification on a teenager\'s phone screen' }, { serial: 'S3556', after: 2, alt: 'A health class poster listing the warning signs of grooming' }, { serial: 'S3557', after: 3, alt: 'A mother taking screenshots of messages on her daughter\'s phone' }, { serial: 'S3558', after: 4, alt: 'A detective talking with a mother and daughter at a kitchen table' }, { serial: 'S3559', after: 5, alt: 'A teenage girl setting her social media account to private' }],
  title: 'The modeling offer', art: 'S3554', cast: [],
  alt: 'A teenage girl reading a message on her phone in her bedroom',
  words: [
    'Jordan was fifteen when a message arrived from an account with thousands of followers. A modeling scout, it said, had seen her photos and thought she had real talent.',
    'Over the next week the messages grew warmer. He sent her a gift card, told her she was mature for her age and promised a paid photo shoot in Dallas. He even offered to send a car to pick her up. All she had to do was keep it between them until the contract was ready.',
    'Jordan remembered the warning signs from health class: flattery, gifts, a secret and a meeting far from home. Grooming, her teacher had called it, building trust in order to exploit it. Real agencies do not ask a fifteen-year-old to hide a job from her parents.',
    'She showed her mother the whole conversation that night. Her mother took screenshots, reported the account to the platform and called the National Human Trafficking Hotline, which helped them report it to the police.',
    'The account disappeared within a day. A detective later told them that the same profile had contacted dozens of girls across Texas, offering the same shoot in the same city. He said that telling a parent right away is the single most useful thing a teenager can do.',
    'Jordan still posts photos, but her account is private now. She has a rule she plans to teach her younger sister: anyone who needs you to keep a secret from your parents is not on your side.',
  ],
};
STORIES['sti-prevention-9'] = {
  about: 'a teenager who planned to say nothing, a vaccine he missed at twelve, infections without symptoms, a CDC chart, and a poster about prenatal care',
  more: [{ serial: 'S3561', after: 1, alt: 'A doctor reviewing a teenager\'s vaccine record with his father' }, { serial: 'S3562', after: 2, alt: 'A doctor explaining how a vaccine works to a teenager' }, { serial: 'S3563', after: 3, alt: 'A doctor showing a CDC chart to a father and son' }, { serial: 'S3564', after: 4, alt: 'A prenatal care poster on a clinic wall' }, { serial: 'S3565', after: 5, alt: 'A father and his teenage son talking in a car outside a clinic' }],
  title: 'The checkup', art: 'S3560', cast: [],
  alt: 'A teenager and his father in a doctor\'s waiting room',
  words: [
    'Ethan was fifteen and annoyed to be at the doctor\'s office on a Saturday. His father had made the appointment for his yearly physical, and Ethan planned to say as little as possible.',
    'The doctor checked his height, weight and blood pressure, then looked at his record. He had missed the HPV vaccine at twelve, she said, and it was not too late to catch up. The vaccine prevents infections that can cause several cancers, including cancers of the throat in men.',
    'Ethan asked why he needed a shot for something he did not have. That was the point, she said: the vaccine works best before any exposure. Many infections, including most STIs, cause no symptoms at all, so people pass them on without knowing.',
    'She showed them a chart from the CDC. Young people ages 15 to 24 account for about half of the new STIs in the United States each year. Testing, she explained, is how infections without symptoms are found and treated.',
    'On the way out, Ethan noticed a poster about prenatal care: if signs of pregnancy appear, tell a parent or trusted adult, get tested early and start care early. His father said that Ethan\'s mother had started prenatal visits the same week she found out about Ethan.',
    'In the car, Ethan admitted the shot had barely hurt. His father said the hardest part of most health decisions is not the needle. It is asking the question in the first place, and Ethan had asked a good one.',
  ],
};
STORIES['choices-and-responsibilities-9'] = {
  about: 'a father of twenty-two who speaks to a health class, an Acknowledgment of Paternity, fourteen more years of child support, and the numbers on effectiveness',
  more: [{ serial: 'S3567', after: 1, alt: 'A young father showing a photo of his daughter to a high school class' }, { serial: 'S3568', after: 2, alt: 'An Acknowledgment of Paternity form on a hospital clipboard' }, { serial: 'S3569', after: 3, alt: 'A young man paying a bill on his phone at a kitchen table' }, { serial: 'S3570', after: 4, alt: 'A health teacher pointing to an effectiveness chart on a classroom screen' }, { serial: 'S3571', after: 5, alt: 'A young man and his older cousin talking on a porch' }],
  title: 'What Darnell wishes he had known', art: 'S3566', cast: [],
  alt: 'A young father in a work uniform holding his four-year-old daughter\'s hand',
  words: [
    'Darnell was twenty-two. He worked nights at a distribution center and took classes at the community college during the day. He was also the father of a four-year-old girl named Kiara, and he had asked to speak to his younger brother\'s health class.',
    'He told the class that he loved his daughter more than anything, and that he still wished he had waited. He had been eighteen and a senior when Kiara\'s mother told him she was pregnant. Both of them finished high school, barely.',
    'Then he explained the parts nobody had told him. In Texas, both parents are legally responsible for supporting their child. He had signed an Acknowledgment of Paternity at the hospital, which made him Kiara\'s legal father, and a court set the child support he pays every month.',
    'That support will continue until Kiara turns eighteen or graduates from high school, whichever comes later. He did the math for the class: it was a bill he would pay for most of the next fourteen years, and he was proud to pay it.',
    'A student asked whether birth control would have changed things. Darnell said the health teacher could give the numbers better than he could. With typical use, about 7 in 100 people relying on the pill and about 13 in 100 relying on condoms become pregnant in a year. Abstinence is the only method that is 100 percent effective.',
    'Before he left, he said the most useful thing anyone did for him was his older cousin telling him that he could choose differently from then on. He did, and he hoped they would make their own choices with their eyes open.',
  ],
};
export const STORY_WORD_LIMIT = { early: 200, older: 350 };
export function storyFor(moduleId) { return STORIES[moduleId] || null; }

